IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`

-- The time-limited money and deposit duties of ss 241, 242, 249 and 249A as regulative rules: PARTY ... MUST ... WITHIN n.
-- Each is the same duty as the decision function of the same provision (`s N the person making the offer has paid ...`), written once more as a rule so that the breach path (the deadline missed) is exercised by a #TRACE.
-- The text states the time limit and not a consequence of its own: the rule ends in FULFILLED when the act is done in time and in BREACH when the time runs out. No consequence is invented.
-- WITHIN counts days from the start of the rule (AT 0 is the day the time runs from: the receipt of the notification, the stop order, the registration), so an act on day n is in time (fork F9).

DECLARE `s 241 duty action` IS ONE OF
    `s 241(10) pay the applicant all moneys paid on account of the application`
    `s 241(11) pay the applicant all moneys paid for the securities or contracts`
    `s 241(13) pay the applicant all moneys paid on account of the application`
    `s 241(14) pay the applicant all moneys paid for the securities or contracts`

DECLARE `s 242 duty action` IS ONE OF
    `s 242(5)(a)(ii) pay the applicants all moneys paid on account of their applications`
    `s 242(5)(b)(ii) pay the applicants all moneys paid for the securities or contracts`
    `s 242(7)(a)(ii) pay the applicants all moneys paid for the securities or contracts`
    `s 242(7)(b)(ii) pay the applicants all moneys paid for the securities or contracts`

DECLARE `s 249 duty action` IS ONE OF
    `s 249(1A) deposit a true copy of every written consent`
    `s 249A(4) deposit a true copy of every written consent`

-- s 241(10): the person making the offer must pay the applicant within 7 days from the receipt of the notification.
-- src:39371 | (10) An applicant who wishes to exercise the applicant’s option
-- src:39372 | under subsection (8)(a)(i) or (ii) to withdraw the applicant’s
-- src:39373 | application must, within 14 days from the date of lodgment of the
-- src:39374 | supplementary document or replacement document, notify the person
-- src:39375 | making the offer of this, upon which that person must, within 7 days
-- src:39376 | from the receipt of such notification, pay to the applicant all moneys
-- src:39377 | paid by the applicant on account of the applicant’s application for the
-- src:39378 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts.
@ref s 241(10) (the duty as a rule) (src:39371-39378)
-- FORK F74 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
GIVEN `the person making the offer` IS A Party @desc Who makes the offer?
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 241 duty action`
`s 241(10) the person making the offer must pay the applicant within 7 days from the receipt of the notification` MEANS
    PARTY `the person making the offer`
    MUST `s 241(10) pay the applicant all moneys paid on account of the application`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person making the offer` BECAUSE "the act was not done within 7 days; the text states the time limit and no consequence of its own"

-- s 241(11): the person making the offer must pay the applicant within 7 days from the receipt of the notification and documents.
-- src:39382 | (11) An applicant who wishes to exercise the applicant’s option
-- src:39383 | under subsection (8)(b)(i) or (ii) to return securities or
-- src:39384 | securities‑based derivatives contracts issued to the applicant must,
-- src:39385 | within 14 days from the date of lodgment of the supplementary
-- src:39386 | document or replacement document, notify the person making the
-- src:39387 | offer of this and return all documents (if any) purporting to be
-- src:39388 | evidence of title to those securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:39389 | contracts to that person, upon which that person must, within 7 days
-- src:39390 | from the receipt of such notification and documents (if any) pay to the
-- src:39391 | applicant all moneys paid by the applicant for the securities or
-- src:39392 | securities‑based derivatives contracts, and the issue of those
-- src:39393 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts is deemed to be
-- src:39394 | void.
@ref s 241(11) (the duty as a rule) (src:39382-39394)
